[32m+[m[32m        <h4>MEANS OF CURRICULUM DELIVERY</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul class="is-goals-list" style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Outcomes-Based Education (OBE):</strong> The curriculum focuses on acquiring specific, measurable skills in law enforcement, criminalistics, and justice administration.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Flexible Learning Modalities:</strong> Depending on school resources, this includes online classes, modular approaches, and traditional classroom settings.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Professional Laboratory & Forensic Studies:</strong> Intensive practical training in forensic photography, crime scene investigation, and lie detection techniques.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Practicum 1 & 2 (Internship):</strong> A compulsory 540-hour on-the-job training program that provides students with practical exposure to police operations, jail management, and fire safety (6 credit units).</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Simulation Exercises:</strong> Use of mock or moot court presentations to develop testimonial skills.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
