[32m+[m[32m        <h3>PHILOSOPHY</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>New Era College of Education embraces excellence, competence, commitments, and professionalism as components of success in training responsible teachers and citizens of the world.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>VISION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>A teacher training institution that produces globally competitive educators imbued with Christian Values, discipline and lifelong service to mankind.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>MISSION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Provide equality education anchored on Christian values with the prime purpose of bringing honor and glory to God.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>GOALS</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul class="is-goals-list" style="list-style-type: decimal;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Train would-be teachers to become morally upright whose Christian values are essential in serving the country and humanity for the glory and honor of the Almighty God.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Strengthen the higher order thinking skills of would-be teachers by providing them with appropriate learning tasks, experiences, and environment.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Upgrade the competencies of would-be teachers for the utilization of effective learning delivery systems and assessment strategies.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Equip would-be teachers with new knowledge through the conduct of functional and quality research works to meet the needs of 21st Century global partners.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Sustain and strengthen Community Outreach Programs responsive to the needs of the partner communities, especially the deprived, depressed, and other under-privileged members of society and other stakeholders.</li>[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="inner-tab-content" id="ced-history" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>HISTORY AND PROFILE</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <img src="assets/images/webp/fac8.webp" alt="College of Education Students and Faculty" style="width:100%; border-radius:4px; margin-bottom: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The College of Education (CED) was established in 1983 and has been one of the foremost colleges at the New Era University. It is a Center of Teacher Training for students who plan to become teachers in the future. It is a home base to some undergraduate organizations, which serve as training grounds for students' planning and leadership skills. Its mother organization, the Educators' Alliance Developing an Optimum Service (EducADOS) supervises the conduct of activities sponsored by CED's umbrella student organizations. These clubs are the following:</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>GENESIS: the organization for all BEEd students<br>SMART: a club for those majoring in Mathematics and Science</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>At present, the CED offers degrees for two programs:<br>[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bachelor of Elementary Education (BEEd) and Bachelor of Secondary Education (BSEd)</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>There are three degrees under BEEd Program, namely:</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul style="margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 15px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Elementary Education (BEEd)</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Elementary Education with Specialization in Early Childhood Education (BEEd - ECEd)</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Elementary Education with Specialization in Inclusive and Special Needs Education (BEEd - SNEd)</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>For BSEd, there are seven degrees that are currently offered:</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul style="margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 15px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in English (BSE - English)</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in Filipino</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in Mathematics</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in Social Studies</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in Science</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in MAPE</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Bachelor of Secondary Education, Major in Technology and Livelihood Education</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Tracing the CED's historical background, it was in 1985, when it started as an Institute merged with the Institute of Arts and Sciences. The Institute of Education as it was formerly called was primarily led by Dr. Amanda Magsino as its first dean.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>By 1988, the Institute of Education (IEd) was separated from the initial merger. This newly separated, independent IEd was led by Dr. Zenaida Soriano. When Dr. Soriano took a leave to work abroad, Dr. Francisca P. Reyes was assigned as OIC for a while. Dr. Lydia L. Libunao who was then the principal of the Elementary Department took the helm from Dr. Francisca P. Reyes and became the dean. The Institute of Education was renamed to the College of Education upon her appointment. Her stewardship of the college lasted for almost 29 years until her untimely demise in 2019...</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>In 2000, the college put up a laboratory school inside the campus to serve as a laboratory school for further train future teachers. This was an innovation initiated when the college was moving higher to its accreditation status...</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>In 2007 the college applied for a permit to operate the ladderized course, Bachelor in Secondary Education Major in Technology and Livelihood Education (BSEd – TLE), and Expanded Tertiary Education Equivalency and Accreditation Program (ETEEAP) programs...</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The College of Education leaped in its level in March 2008 and became a Center of Teacher Training Institution (COTTI). That was earned in its Level III Accreditation visitation by the PACUCOA (Philippine Association of Colleges and Universities Commission on Accreditation) on October 19-20, 2015.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Since then, the College of Education has continued to produce licensed teachers, even topnotchers. Among the topnotchers of the Licensure Examination for Teachers (LET) were Dr. Liliabeth P. Taa (a CED faculty) who got the 1st place in the 1996 board exam, and this was followed by Ms. Celia Concepcion O. Gregorio who also ranked 1st in 2000, and the most recent, Mr. Dante V. Dela Merced who clinched the 2nd place in August 2014.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>In 2019, Dr. Corazon V. Uwayway, the associate dean, took over the helm. It was during the stewardship of Dr. Uwayway that the College of Education revitalized its marketing efforts to motivate and encourage more students to enroll in the college...</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Year 2020, the pandemic and a new normal in education and learning set in. Seven (7) faculty members took a leave, while others retired. With this, the College of Education welcomed new blood, faculty members who were younger and technology-savvy... Students from different parts of the world were able to pursue their education and avail the new learning modality which can be accessed through this improved technology.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>With the new normal, the school calendar underwent changes as well. The CED graduating class had their virtual commencement exercises before the year ended.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Furthermore, this pandemic brought the heroic deed of the NEU Alumni Association officers... These AAs were the basis for the provision of teacher salaries.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Year 2021, the year started with an aid given to faculty members and staff to at least ease the effect of the pandemic... The CED even spearheaded the Book Writing project of the school, where the teachers in the Integrated School were encouraged and motivated to write their own books in the subjects they have been teaching...</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The CED is known as a high performing institution in the field of education. It is a Center for Teacher Training, and produces graduates who are employed as private and public school teachers in the National Capital Region...</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The College of Education (CED) has a roster of highly qualified teachers and professors who are seasoned practitioners in the academe. It has a track record of high passing rate in the Board Examinations which is over and above that of the national passing rate. As it was granted a Level 3 Re-accredited status by PACUCOA in 2019, the College of Education, hopefully will apply as a Center for Excellence in the field of Teacher Education soon.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="inner-tab-content" id="ced-seal" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>THE COLLEGE SEAL</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <img src="assets/images/webp/College%20Seals/CED-college-seal.webp" alt="CED Official Logo" style="width: 50%; margin:0 auto">[m
[32m+[m[32m        </div>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The seal of the New Era University - College of Education serves as a visual testament to its mission of nurturing future educators through a synthesis of faith and academic excellence. At its heart, the design features an open book and a burning torch flanked by laurel leaves, symbolizing the illumination of the mind and the triumph of scholarly pursuit. These elements are set against the backdrop of a radiant sun rays, while representing the dawn of a new era in learning.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>True to its core identity, the emblem is anchored by the year 1983, marking the college's historical foundation. Every symbol within the circular frame is unified by the institution's guiding philosophy: "Godliness is the foundation of Knowledge." This profound principle suggests that true intellectual mastery is inseparable from spiritual integrity, ensuring that the educators produced within these halls are not only technically proficient but also morally grounded leaders dedicated to the service of humanity.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="inner-tab-content" id="ced-curriculum" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>CURRICULUM</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The Bachelor of Elementary Education (BEEd) curriculum, governed by CHED Memorandum Order (CMO) No. 74, series of 2017, is a four-year outcomes-based program training teachers for Grades 1-6. It consists of General Education, Professional Education, and specialization courses (Major courses) totaling 120+ units, focusing on content knowledge, pedagogical skills, and field study, aimed at developing K-12 compliant educators.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The Bachelor of Secondary Education (BSEd) however, in the Philippines is a 4-year degree program under CHED Memorandum Order 75, s. 2017 aimed at preparing high school teachers. The curriculum focuses on Outcomes-Based Education (OBE), consisting of general education, professional education, and specialized major subjects, culminating in a final year teaching internship.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h4 style="margin-top: 25px;">PROGRAM OUTCOMES</h4>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h5>For BEEd:</h5>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul class="is-goals-list">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Content Mastery & Pedagogy:</strong> Exhibit in-depth understanding of elementary learners and pedagogical content knowledge across subject areas.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Learning Facilitation:</strong> Facilitate learning using diverse methodologies, technology, and assessment tools.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Curriculum Development:</strong> Develop innovative curricula, instructional plans, and materials for diverse learners.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Professionalism:</strong> Demonstrate positive attributes of a model teacher, including lifelong learning, and adhere to ethical standards.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Research and Mentorship:</strong> Engage in research to improve educational practices.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h5>For BSEd:</h5>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul class="is-goals-list">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Knowledge and Understanding:</strong> Demonstrate in-depth understanding of the development of adolescent learners. Exhibit comprehensive knowledge of various learning areas in the secondary curriculum. Articulate the relationship of education to historical, social, cultural, and political processes.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Teaching Skills and Pedagogical Knowledge:</strong> Apply a wide range of teaching process skills (curriculum development, lesson planning, materials development, and educational assessment). Facilitate learning using diverse methodologies and specialized teaching approaches for diverse learners. Utilize appropriate technologies to enhance teaching and learning.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Professionalism and Personal Growth:</strong> Practice professional and ethical standards of the teaching profession. Reflect on teaching practices to improve teaching knowledge and skills. Pursue lifelong learning for personal and professional growth.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li><strong>Skills in Research and Leadership:</strong> Show scholarship in research and further learning. Demonstrate leadership skills to help in teaching and community empowerment. Integrate local and global perspectives in teaching, including principles of sustainable development.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
