[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>VISION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>A community of scholars and educators engaged in the application of the science and art of midwifery promoting health across all types of clientele  in maternal and child care.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>MISSION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Breed knowledge through research in midwifery, health and interdisciplinary science, educate leaders in midwifery to advance healthcare locally and globally, provide innovative and exemplary health care and shape future midwives through leadership in healthcare policy.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>GOALS</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The college of Midwifery fulfills its mission by meeting the following goals:</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul class="is-goals-list" style="list-style-type: decimal;">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Offer a degree to prepare individuals for career opportunities to practice as a direct-entry midwife who provides primary maternal and childcare.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Provide a curriculum core competencies and student support services that provide opportunities to acquire knowledge skills and attributes compatible to the practice of midwifery.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Prepare graduates to practice as direct-entry midwives and provide primary care to mothers and children.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Nurture a culture of scholarship and contribution to the discipline to enhance the profession and knowledge of midwifery.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Engage in inter-professional relationship, collaborative research and clinical partnership to optimize student learning.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="inner-tab-content" id="cmw-history" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>HISTORY AND PROFILE</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <img src="assets/images/webp/student-image%20%286%29.webp" alt="College of Midwifery Students and Faculty" style="width:100%; border-radius:4px; margin-bottom: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The College of Midwifery (CMW) at New Era University was established in 2015 as a dedicated degree-granting unit committed to producing competent, compassionate, and globally competitive midwifery professionals.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h4>Our Program</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>We offer a comprehensive Bachelor of Science in Midwifery program that provides a strong foundation for the Midwifery degree.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h4>Outstanding Board Performance</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Our commitment to academic excellence is reflected in our impressive 83.33% passing rate in the November 2017 Licensure Examination for Midwives. We are especially proud of Miss Mary Anne Silverio, who ranked 4th place nationwide with a rating of 88%.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h4>Professional Affiliations</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>The College of Midwifery is an active member of the Association of Philippine Schools of Midwifery, Inc. (APSOM), connecting us with a network of leading midwifery education institutions across the Philippines.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Our students gain a deep understanding of how midwifery knowledge, skills, and attitudes can create positive, life-changing impact on the health and survival of mothers and babies—not only in the Philippines but around the world.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h4>Curriculum Excellence</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Our comprehensive curriculum integrates general education and professional courses, equipping students with entry-level midwifery competencies through:</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <h5>Core Clinical Practicums:</h5>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <ul class="is-goals-list" style="list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Foundations of Midwifery</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Normal Obstetrics and Care of the Newborn</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Pathologic Obstetrics</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Primary Health Care</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Midwifery Ethics and Law</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h4>Licensure Preparation</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Graduates of our program are fully qualified to take the government licensure examination and begin their careers as registered midwives.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="inner-tab-content" id="cmw-seal" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <h3>THE COLLEGE SEAL</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m            <img src="assets/images/webp/College%20Seals/CMW-college-seal.webp" alt="CMW Official Logo" style="width: 50%; margin:0 auto">[m
[32m+[m[32m        </div>[m
[32m+[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Within the framework of New Era University (green and red borders), established in 2015, the College of Midwifery is illuminated by Filipino national pride and the light of knowledge (sun).</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>Grounded in rigorous academic learning (book), midwifery students are prepared to provide compassionate, evidence-based care to mothers and children (mother-infant figure), upholding the values of life, growth, and professional excellence.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <p>In essence, this logo successfully merges national identity, professional healthcare symbolism, and educational mission into a cohesive, meaningful visual representation of the College of Midwifery's values and purpose.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
