[32m+[m[32m            <li>Outcomes-Based Education (OBE): The curriculum is organized around what learners should know, value, and be able to do, ensuring they meet the required level of competence for midwifery practice.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m            <li>Clinical Practicum (RLE): A massive portion of the curriculum is dedicated to hands-on training. The 4-year BSM program requires intensive clinical practicum, with 53 units specifically dedicated to clinical practice (2,346 hours).</li>[m
