[32m+[m[32m                <div class="inner-tab-content" id="coc-vmo" style="display: block;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>VISION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The College of Communication envisions itself as an excellent education institution in media and communication</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>MISSION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The College of Communication provides quality education based on communication research, collaborative partnerships and linkages, and excellent multimedia professional practice strongly anchored on Christian culture.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>GOALS</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ol class="cics-goals-list" style="padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Establish the College as a distinguished Center of Development and Center of Excellence.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Engage in dynamic teaching and learning methodologies in the fields of media and communication.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Develop and produce communication research and creative works as well as innovations in all aspects of media and communication.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Strengthen academic leadership among students and faculty through continuing professional competencies development.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Adapt to the dynamic and overarching environment from local, national, and global media and communication landscapes.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Empower the Media and Communication students to become socially responsive to the needs of the community and society.</li>[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ol>[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                <div class="inner-tab-content" id="coc-history" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>HISTORY AND PROFILE</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <img src="assets/images/webp/student-image%20%284%29.webp" alt="College of Communication Students and Faculty" style="width:100%; border-radius:4px; margin-bottom: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>In 1979, New Era University launched the Bachelor of Arts – Major in Mass Communication under the College of Arts and Sciences as a part of the Liberal Arts Program. This paved the way for the eventual foundation of the College of Communication (COC), which was founded on the 17th of July, 2014. The College was established at the same time as the Bachelor of Arts in Communication program. In October 2015, the Liberal Arts program was granted Level III Accreditation Status.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>To celebrate its vibrant and talented students, conducted the highly anticipated Comm Awards for the first time at the Professional Schools Building on the 3rd of April 2017. Different genres of art and communication melded to showcase the full spectrum of skills students have acquired and honed. COC Alumni arrived to show their full support.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>On July 7, 2017, the College of Communication ushered in the new academic year with the orientation program titled "Kabida Level Up," spearheaded by the Communicator's Guild Officers. A month later, on August 29, COC commenced with the traditional General Assembly, which gained renown as the "Best GA Ever" from aggregated student responses.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>In a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity, thirty (30) delegates from the College of Communication were chosen to attend "The 1st Southeast Asia Prix Jeunesse" video film festival for children held at The Peninsula, Manila. The delegates watched various films from different ASEAN countries to celebrate the unique cinematic voices of young filmmakers.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The BA Broadcasting and BA Journalism Programs were established to join the College of Communication's academic roster alongside the BA Communication in 2018. In January 2024, the Commission on Higher Education (CHED), led by Chairperson Sharn Baluyot, officially recognized both the Bachelor of Arts in Broadcasting and the Bachelor of Arts in Journalism.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>Several years after separating from the College of Arts and Sciences, the College of Communication proved that it could stand and prosper as a separate entity, navigating challenges and emerging triumphant.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                <div class="inner-tab-content" id="coc-seal" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>THE COLLEGE SEAL</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <img src="assets/images/webp/College%20Seals/COC-college-seal.webp" alt="COC Official Logo" style="width: 50%; margin:0 auto">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </div>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The official logo of COC follows the standard wherein the emblem and the upper portion (rising sun) symbolize the identity of the University. The other half of the logo represents the College. The signal waves before the letter "C" indicates the nature of communication which is sending verbal and non-verbal messages through diverse media platforms. It also indicates the dynamism of the discipline of Communication.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>While the colors of the signal waves: green, white, and red connotes the adherence of the college to the Philosophy, Vision and Mission of the University in providing quality education to the students.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>In the logo, letter "C" is very prominent which stands for "Communication." It is also in color blue text which is adapted to the official color of the Iglesia Ni Cristo Centennial Celebration (2014), the same year when the College was established.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                <div class="inner-tab-content" id="coc-curriculum" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>CURRICULUM</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The curriculum for BA Communication includes general education courses, core courses, required courses, electives, and thesis/special project. Courses that would generate a particular track, concentration, or area specialization may also be offered.</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4 style="margin-top: 25px;">PROGRAM OUTCOMES</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ol class="cics-goals-list" style="padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Advocate Christian values and practices in implementing and pursuing the Discipline of Communication.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate service-oriented capacity, ability, and competency at all times.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Uphold proficiency in facilitating learning through multi-literacies, conforming and adapting to the dynamism of the Communication process.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Understand the use and management of technology in the delivery of information with utmost care.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Develop and produce communication research and creative works, as well as innovations in all aspects of Communication.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Apply the scientific and creative minds for the improvement of the community.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Practice effective communication in different formats and platforms.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Conduct accurate and successful conveying of messages.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Cooperate with the stakeholders to attain meaningful advocacies utilizing effectual communication process.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Practice leadership and collaborative potentials to achieve the best results.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Pursue lifelong learning with the full determination for the betterment of oneself and in being with others.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate development orientation and entrepreneurial capabilities in communication work.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Know and practice rights, responsibilities, and accountabilities in the Communication profession.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Adhere to ethics, professionalism, and social responsibility in Communication practices</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ol>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4 style="margin-top: 25px;">MEANS OF CURRICULUM DELIVERY</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ul class="cics-goals-list">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Outcomes-Based Education (OBE):</strong> The delivery is driven by desired student learning outcomes, ensuring proficiency in communication theories, research, and production.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Practical/Creative Workshops:</strong> Hands-on training in print, broadcast, and online media platforms.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Case Studies and Simulation:</strong> Analysis of real-world communication scenarios and professional ethical dilemmas.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Internship/Practicum:</strong> Mandatory industry immersion to develop professional competence.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Individual and Team Projects:</strong> Development of media campaigns, research papers, and creative audio/visual projects.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Flexible Modalities:</strong> Institutions may blend traditional classroom, online, or hybrid learning to suit student needs and institutional strengths</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
