[32m+[m[32m                <div class="inner-tab-content" id="com-curriculum" style="display: none;">[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>CURRICULUM</h3>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The Bachelor of Music (BM) program in the Philippines, as aligned with CHED Memorandum Order (CMO) No. 82, Series of 2017, is a four-to-five-year degree focused on professional music training. It includes General Education (GE) courses, core music theory, music history, performance (major instrument/voice), and specialization electives. The curriculum follows a, learner-centered, outcomes-based approach</p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4 style="margin-top: 25px;">PROGRAM OUTCOMES</h4>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ul class="is-goals-list">[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate profound internalization and application of Christian values in applied fields of musical endeavor.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate exemplary levels of service through performance, teaching, and research.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Produce music unique to today's world through the innovative application of modern technology, 21st century skills, and multi literacies.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Push the artistic boundaries of modern music - making.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate fluid communication through effective ensemble building, conducting, instruction, interpersonal skills, and developing the social skills needed to convey musical objectives.</li>[m
[32m+[m[41m                        [m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Lead and collaborate in the formulation and planning of musical and creative projects that create lasting impact.</li>[m
[32m+[m[41m                        [m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate commitment as a lifelong student of music.</li>[m
[32m+[m[41m                        [m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Demonstrate ethics, sound professionalism, and good Christian upbringing in all facets of life and artistic endeavor.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ul>[m
[32m+[m[41m            [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4>MEANS OF CURRICULUM DELIVERY</h4>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ul class="is-goals-list">[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Outcomes-Based Education (OBE): Curricula are focused on specific learning outcomes, including mastery of subject matter, critical musical thinking, and the use of technology.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Flexible Learning: In response to modern needs, institutions use a blend of in-person studio instruction, classroom lectures, and online platforms.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Practical Application: Performance majors are required to hold public recitals, while Music Education majors undergo field observations in schools.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Technology Integration: Music programs integrate computer applications for notation, recording, and composition.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ul>[m
