[32m+[m[32m                        <h4>PROGRAM OUTCOMES</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <p style="padding-left: 10px; margin-top: 10px;">By the time of graduation, students are equipped to:</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <ul class="is-goals-list" style="padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <li>Compare, contrast, and classify major concepts, theories, and subfields in political science.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <li>Design and execute research inquiries using appropriate quantitative and qualitative methods.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <li>Demonstrate written, visual, and oral presentation skills for analytical reports.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <li>Analyze and respond to national/global political issues using historical and contemporary perspectives.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <li>Develop a predisposition toward ethical political involvement and professional engagement.</li>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4> PROGRAM GOALS</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The Bachelor in Public Administration Programs prepares students for careers in government, both in politics and in government service. It aims to equip the students with the right ethical standards which they will need in the government service.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <ul class="is-goals-list" style="padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <p>1. Aims to create an ethical man who is ready, willing and able to sacrifice his own desires to promote the public welfare and the economic progress of the nation as a Whole.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <p>2. Develop leadership, analytical, organizational, research and communication skills, prepared to enter fields in the private and public sector.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <p>3. Enable the students to have a sense of noble purpose in serving the country. Formulate ethical principles applicable to every aspect of the government service and to have the moral courage to implement the proper moral sense into every aspect of government service.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <p>4. Competency to learn continuously throughout their life that will enable them to live meaningfully in a challenging, rapidly changing, and globalized world while engaging in their community and the nation's development issues and concerns.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <p>5. Implement complex public programs, while troubleshooting community and governmental issues successfully. Learned business management techniques and the moral implications behind those actions so that programs can function effectively.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                            <p>6. Prepare graduates of such programs go on to find jobs in the public sector or pursue advanced degrees.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4> COMPETENCY STANDARDS</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ul class="is-goals-list" style="padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Deep understanding of good governance, public policy, and administrative theories.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Proficiency in planning, implementing, monitoring, and evaluating public services, alongside human and material resource management.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>High dedication to public interest, accountability, nationalism, and serving marginalized communities.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Capacity to conduct research for evidence-based decision-making and policy formulation.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li>Effective communication and interpersonal skills for various stakeholders.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ul>[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h4>CARREER OPPORTUNITIES</h4>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>There are several career paths that BPA graduates can choose as future administrators:</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                     <ul class="is-goals-list" style="padding-left: 20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <p>1. Researcher - BAPA graduates may find themselves needed in both fields of public and private administration. Practically, all professional undertakings need research as life continues to improve. As in the case of public administration, more pertinent issues, policies, and practices are changing based on the recommendations of experienced practioneers and researchers in this field.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <p>2. Education - BAPA graduates can be educators who will share their knowledge and enjoy working with students in the classroom, in their office and in the field.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <p>3. Administrator - BAPA graduates are also equip with the needed tools and qualifications to work as administrators primarily in the government and in private business management as well.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ul>[m[41m  [m
