[32m+[m[32m            <div id="history" class="content-section" style="display: block;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                <h2 class="content-title">HISTORY</h2>[m
[32m+[m[41m                [m
[32m+[m[32m                <div class="history-content">[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <img src="../assets/images/webp/concamp2.webp" alt="NEU Lipa Campus History Image 1" class="history-image" style="margin-top: 0;">[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>New Era University - Lipa City Branch is located at 1795 P. Olan St., Marawoy, Lipa City, Batangas, about 6.5-km[m
[32m+[m[32maway or 17-minute drive from Batangas North District which is located at Lipa City Local Congregation, the center[m
[32m+[m[32mlocal of the district. Before the new school year opened, Bro. Buenaventura de Castro (Resident Minister,[m
[32m+[m[32mLipa City Locale) called for Sister Leticia Ramos Rocafort (District NFE Coordinator at the DepEd Lipa City Division[m
[32m+[m[32mOffice) to meet with Dr. Corazon C. Osorio and her colleagues at the Pastoral House. She was then tasked to secure[m
[32m+[m[32mpertinent papers, and to interview and meticulously screen the incoming teachers, staff, and support service[m
[32m+[m[32mpersonnel.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <img src="../assets/images/webp/eN1Bw.webp" alt="NEU Lipa Campus History Image 2" class="history-image">[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>New Era University - Lipa City Branch was established on May 5, 2000, [3] under the leadership of Brother Eraño G.[m
[32m+[m[32mManalo, the Executive Minister of the Church Of Christ, from 1963 to 2009. Its inauguration was part of the New Era[m
[32m+[m[32mUniversity Main Campus' Silver Jubilee celebration, a milestone that is worthy to magnify. The New Era University[m
[32m+[m[32mLipa City Branch was established primarily to give glory to the Lord God Almighty and to accommodate the needs[m
[32m+[m[32mof the members of the Church Of Christ not only in the cognitive aspect but especially in the need to fully preserve[m
[32m+[m[32mheir faith.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>On its first operating year, there were one hundred eighty-five (185) pupils in the pre-school and elementary[m
[32m+[m[32mdepartment, eight (8) administrative officials, and twelve (12) faculty members. The first Branch Director was Brother[m
[32m+[m[32mAlberto R. Domingo Jr., a Minister and educator.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>High school curriculum was offered during its second year of operation [4] having one hundred sixty-five enrollees[m
[32m+[m[32m(165), two hundred thirteen (213) in the elementary , and forty-nine (49) in the pre-school for a total of four hundred[m
[32m+[m[32mtwenty-seven (427) pupils and students. It was doubled compared to the previous year. Thirteen (13) high school[m
[32m+[m[32mfaculty members were added.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>In the seventh year of the school, the most essential edifice was established - the chapel of the New Era Local[m
[32m+[m[32mCongregation. It was approved on September 07, 2007 and was dedicated to God on September 15, 2007 by[m
[32m+[m[32mBrother Bienvenido C. Santiago. It was a 500-seater house of worship service to accommodate the branch's spiritual[m
[32m+[m[32mneeds.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The official newsletter of the branch "Ugnayan" was launched during the Academic Year 2008-2009. Students to a[m
[32m+[m[32mcertain extent were pretty excited to showcase their writing capacities and ingenuity through feature and news[m
[32m+[m[32mwriting. It was on April 3, 2009 when the school started to extend its service to children with Special needs.[m
[32m+[m[32mAcademic year 2015-2016 when the school offered courses in College such as Accountancy, Entrepreneurship, Real[m
[32m+[m[32mEstate, and Accounting Technology.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>On July 27, 2014 - The branch gained enormous faith and enthusiasm with all the achievements and world record[m
[32m+[m[32maccomplishments of the currently called 21st Century Church - the IGLESIA NI CRISTO! It made both the Academic[m
[32m+[m[32mand Administrative Council, together with the stakeholders, to collaborate in ensuring the standards for the[m
[32m+[m[32mbranch to be considered as a 21st Century School.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The achievements that the university has received are truly innumerable since its founding year. Currently, it passed[m
[32m+[m[32mthe PACUCOA Level 2 Accredited Status 2022. It has also produced top-notch students. It has received a letter of[m
[32m+[m[32mcommendation given by the most beloved Executive Minister, Brother Eduardo V. Manalo on November 2014 which[m
[32m+[m[32mmade the entire campus more energetic and enormously inspired to perform their duties and obligations to the[m
[32m+[m[32mschool. The school has also been a witness of many struggles just like what happened on the 12th of January 2020[m
[32m+[m[32mwhen the famous Taal Volcano situated in Batangas erupted.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>However, such calamity was never a hindrance for the university to extend its services in helping the community[m
[32m+[m[32msince this is the extension of the Church Administration of the Church Of Christ to fulfill God's command, one of[m
[32m+[m[32mwhich is helping the needy or victims of calamities. New Era University Lipa City Branch served as an evacuation[m
[32m+[m[32marea for hundreds of Batanguenos. Members of the school administration, faculty, and staff volunteered for the Aid[m
[32m+[m[32mto Humanity, a program of the INC's charitable arm, the Felix Y. Manalo Foundation, in distributing the needs of the[m
[32m+[m[32mvictims such as food and medicine.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>As people recover from the damage caused by the volcanic eruption, the world was shaken by the news that the[m
[32m+[m[32mnew deadly disease caused by the virus which later called Covid-19 has spread and reached the Philippines. On[m
[32m+[m[32mMarch 11, 2020 the World Health Organization (WHO) declared a global pandemic. The government declared a[m
[32m+[m[32mtotal lockdown, implemented a minimum health protocol, and temporarily closed various establishments, religious[m
[32m+[m[32mgatherings, and schools.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The university was prompt. Teachers phoned up their students and parents to know their condition. The Church[m
[32m+[m[32mAdministration through Christian Family Organization launched mental health awareness seminars to strengthen[m
[32m+[m[32mthe faith primarily of the brethren and students enrolled in the school. Education has to continue. Different[m
[32m+[m[32mmodalities were suggested. Virtual classroom was created and learning was done through online. This paved way t[m
[32m+[m[32mNEU Virtual Learnning Environment (NEUVLE) wherein students can access their activities using their NEU account[m
[32m+[m[32mLearning went smoothly with the assistance of the diligent and workaholic teachers.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>However, no matter how many storms come, the heart of the university will not change - trust in what the Father can[m
[32m+[m[32mdo and continue to pray to Him. The school continues to serve parents and students whether there is a pandemic[m
[32m+[m[32mor calamity. It continues to help students achieve their dreams with the help of teachers, ministers and workers lec[m
[32m+[m[32mby the present Branch Director, Brother Norman U. Ramos, in acc[m
[32m+[m[32mRamos, in accordance and united with the spirit and aim of the[m
[32m+[m[32mExecutive Minister of the Church Of Christ - Brother Eduardo V. Manalo.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>Prior to this, the Branch Administration and faculty laid their plans for the opening of classes. They prepared the[m
[32m+[m[32mschool by cleaning all the areas, providing materials and facilities as prescribed by the Department of Education.[m
[32m+[m[32mPresently, Lipa's Branch Dlrector is Bro. Beliardo DT. Dote.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>For more than two decades, the School has been a witness to triumphs and trials. But the School believes it will[m
[32m+[m[32mcontinue to exist not because of the people who run the school but because of the guidance of the Lord God</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>Almighty which was the resounding message of the late Brother Erano G.Manalo, the brainchild of NEU-LCB's[m
[32m+[m[32memergence that: "The prime purpose of this school is for the Glory of God. Let no one teach here anything that will[m
[32m+[m[32malienate man from God. Let not this school be the battle- ground of warring students. Let no one destroy the[m
[32m+[m[32mbrotherly love that should exist between teachers and students. Above all, let the implementation and fulfillment of[m
[32m+[m[32mGod's words be the prevailing atmosphere inside this structure where wisdom dwells."</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>On May 05, 2025 the branch reached its 25th anniversary. The administrators and faculty members started planning[m
[32m+[m[32mfor the activities in accordance with the school's mission-vision - to give glory to God and selfless[m
[32m+[m[32mservice to humanity.</p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
