[32m+[m[32m                    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: #333; margin-bottom: 25px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        The University seal bears identifiable images which put into visual symbols the institutional philosophy of <strong>New Era University - Lipa</strong>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </p>[m
[32m+[m[41m                    [m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        The above figure is the Official Logo of the NEW ERA UNIVERSITY - Lipa City Campus approved by the Church Administration of the Iglesia Ni Cristo through the NEU Administration was first adopted and used by the NEU-LCB community.[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        The logo's features retained the overall components of the official NEU logo: <strong>Outer Ring</strong> is Green, <strong>Inner Ring</strong> is Red and <strong>the space color between the rings containing the name of New Era University</strong> is White (Green, White and Red)- the official colors of the INC which is behind the establishment and continuous operations of the University and its branches outside NCR including NEU - Lipa City Branch. Also among the features of the official University logo retained in the official NEU-Lipa City Branch Logo are the <strong>Rising Sun and the Open Book</strong> representing enlightenment and illumination of those who benefit from NEU as an educational institution that imparts values-laden education leading to the total development of an individual.[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        The distinct features original and unique in the NEU-Lipa City Branch official Logo are the following: <strong>Map of the Province of Lipa City</strong> which is made as background of the Open Book and the Rising Sun. This represents the region (Region III) that is primarily being served by the NEU-Pampanga. Provinces within Region III and in proximity to Pampanga province are Bataan, Bulacan, Zambales, and Tarlac. And <strong>2000 - the year when NEU Lipa City Branch was established</strong> as the second branch of NEU outside the NCR, is also indicated in the NEU Lipa City Branch Logo.[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </p>[m
