[32m+[m[32m                <h2 class="content-title">PAYMENT OF FEES</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m                <h3 class="content-subtitle">PAYMENT REMINDERS</h3>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                <div class="content-paragraph">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>Staying on top of your financial obligations is key to a smooth and uninterrupted academic journey. To help you navigate the enrollment process and manage[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m                        your dues effectively, we have compiled a comprehensive list of essential payment reminders covering everything from transaction security to branch-specific[m
[32m+[m[32m                        protocols. Please review these guidelines carefully to ensure your records are accurate, your personal data remains protected under our privacy policy, and your[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m                        focus remains where it matters most-on your studies:[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </p><br>[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
[32m+[m[32m                <ul class="content-list">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Check Your Portal: Regularly log in to your student account to view the most updated balance.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Verify Deadlines: Always refer to the official academic calendar for tuition and miscellaneous fee due dates.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Include Student ID: Ensure your full name and Student ID number are included in all payment transactions.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Confirm Branch Links: Use the specific payment form designated for your branch (e.g., GenSan, Lipa City, Pampanga, or Rizal).</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Secure Your Receipt: Always save a digital or physical copy of your transaction slip for your personal records.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Data Privacy Compliance: Only submit proof of payment through official, secure university channels to protect your personal information.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Clear Uploads: When submitting confirmation forms, ensure photos or scans of receipts are legible and uncropped.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Processing Time: Allow 2 to 3 business days for payments to be validated and reflected in your account.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Avoid Late Fees: Settle balances on or before the deadline to prevent automatic late charges or account holds.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Installment Plans: If you are on an installment scheme, ensure each specific milestone payment is met on time.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>cholarship Credits: Students with scholarships should verify that their grants have been applied before settling the remaining balance.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Check for Emails: Watch for automated confirmation emails once your payment has been successfully processed.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Update Contact Info: Ensure your registered email and phone number are current to receive urgent billing alerts.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Refund Policy: Familiarize yourself with the university's refund and withdrawal policies early in the semester.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Third-Party Fees: Note that some bank transfers or mobile wallets may charge independent transaction fees.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>One Form Per Transaction: Submit a separate confirmation form for every individual payment made.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Enrollment Status: Remember that payment alone does not complete enrollment; you must receive a validated registration form.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Laboratory Fees: Double-check if your specific course requires additional laboratory or technical fees for the current term.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Secure Payment Gateways: Only use university-authorized banks and payment centers listed on the official website.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Audit Your Ledger: At the end of each month, review your ledger for any discrepancies and report them immediately.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Keep Receipts Confidential: Never share photos of your payment receipts on public social media platforms.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Exam Clearance: Ensure all dues are settled at least one week before midterms or finals to secure your permit.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Official Communication: Use your university-issued email for all inquiries sent to the Accounting Office.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Bank Validation: Ensure bank-validated slips are clearly stamped by the teller before leaving the counter.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Check Clearance: For check payments, enrollment is only considered official once the check has cleared.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Back-to-Back Payments: If paying for multiple semesters, specify the breakdown clearly in the remarks section.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Graduation Fees: Graduating students should check for one-time exit fees and clearance requirements.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Authorized Representatives: If a third party is paying on your behalf, they must still use your correct Student ID.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Discrepancy Reporting: If a payment isn't reflected after 5 business days, contact the Finance Department with your proof of payment.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <li>Stay Informed: Read all billing-related announcements posted on the university's official bulletin and social media pages.</li>[m
[32m+[m[41m            [m
[32m+[m[32m                </ul>[m
