[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>VISION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>To cultivate a student body that embodies a Christian character, academic distinction, and a commitment to service, reflecting our unique Christian culture.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>MISSION</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The Office of Student Affairs and Services is dedicated to nurturing the holistic development of students, fostering an environment where "Godliness is the Foundation of Knowledge" by providing Christ-centered programs and services that uphold the university's mission of delivering quality education anchored on Christian values, ultimately bringing honor and glory to God.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>GOALS</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <ul class="is-goals-list">[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Integrate Christian Values:</strong> Embed Christian principles and biblical teachings into all student programs and services.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Foster Spiritual Growth:</strong> Provide opportunities for students to deepen their faith and develop a personal relationship with God.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Promote Academic Excellence:</strong> Support student success through resources and guidance that align with the university's commitment to quality education.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Develop Servant Leaders:</strong> Equip students with the skills and heart for service to humanity, both within and outside the university community.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Cultivate a Culture of Discipline:</strong> Instill in students the importance of self-control, accountability, and ethical conduct.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Enhance Student Well-being:</strong> Offer comprehensive support systems that address the physical, emotional, and social needs of students in a Christ-centered manner.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Build Community:</strong> Create a vibrant and inclusive campus environment that fosters strong relationships and a sense of belonging among students.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                        <li><strong>Uphold University Standards:</strong> Ensure all student activities and behaviors align with the university's vision of excellence and Christian culture.</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    </ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m                </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                <div id="osas-history" class="inner-tab-content" style="display:none;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <h3>BRIEF HISTORY</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The Office of Student Affairs and Services (OSAS) was founded in 1975 with a clear purpose: to be a cornerstone of the university's commitment to holistic education. From its inception, OSAS was tasked with a mission far greater than mere administrative support. Guided by the university's foundational philosophy that "Godliness is the Foundation of Knowledge," the office was created to actively nurture the spiritual, moral, and social well-being of every student. In its early years, OSAS laid the groundwork for a campus culture that sought to integrate Christian values and academic pursuits, ensuring that students were equipped not just with knowledge, but with a character anchored in faith.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <img src="assets/images/webp/010eN.webp" alt="History Banner" style="width:100%; border-radius:4px; margin-bottom:20px;">[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>The Office of Student Affairs and Services (OSAS) was founded in 1975 with a clear purpose: to be a cornerstone of the university's commitment to holistic education. From its inception, OSAS was tasked with a mission far greater than mere administrative support. Guided by the university's foundational philosophy that "Godliness is the Foundation of Knowledge," the office was created to actively nurture the spiritual, moral, and social well-being of every student. In its early years, OSAS laid the groundwork for a campus culture that sought to integrate Christian values and academic pursuits, ensuring that students were equipped not just with knowledge, but with a character anchored in faith.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>As the university grew, so too did the role of the OSAS. Over the decades, the office's programs and services expanded to meet the evolving needs of a diverse student body, always remaining faithful to its core mission. It became the primary driver in cultivating the "unique Christian culture of excellence, discipline, and service to humanity" envisioned by the university. Through the development of leadership programs, spiritual formation activities, and comprehensive support systems, OSAS worked to create an environment where students could thrive, learn to serve, and embrace the principles of accountability and compassion.</p>[m
[32m+[m[32m                    <p>Today, the Office of Student Affairs and Services stands as a testament to its enduring legacy. It continues to serve as the heart of student life, upholding the traditions established in 1975 while innovating to meet modern challenges. The office remains dedicated to its original purpose: to support students in their journey toward becoming world-class individuals who are disciplined in character, excellent in their chosen fields, and committed to bringing honor and glory to God through service. The OSAS is not just a department; it is a living expression of the university's mission and vision, shaping the next generation of Christian leaders.</p>[m
